# Request collection for the service, in the plain-text .http format that
# editors such as VS Code (REST Client) and JetBrains IDEs run.
# Start the service first (make start), then send a request.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081

### Liveness probe: 200 with the body "pong"
GET {{baseUrl}}/ping

### Health check: 204 without a body, or a 500 problem document that lists the failing dependencies
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### List the resources, newest first; page starts at 1, itemsPerPage is 1 to 100 (a bare JSON array)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/example_api_resources?page=1&itemsPerPage=30

### Create a resource: 201 with the resource and a location header; 422 when validation fails
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/example_api_resources
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Example name",
  "description": "Example description"
}

### Retrieve one resource by identifier: 200, 400 for an invalid identifier, 404 when it does not exist
# Replace the identifier with the id returned by the create request.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/example_api_resources/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe

### GraphQL query: one page of resources (page and itemsPerPage have defaults)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($page: Int!, $itemsPerPage: Int!) { exampleApiResources(page: $page, itemsPerPage: $itemsPerPage) { id name description } }",
  "variables": { "page": 1, "itemsPerPage": 30 }
}

### GraphQL query: one resource by id (null when it does not exist)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($id: ID!) { exampleApiResource(id: $id) { id name description } }",
  "variables": { "id": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe" }
}

### GraphQL mutation: create a resource
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation ($input: CreateExampleApiResourceInput!) { createExampleApiResource(input: $input) { id name description } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "name": "Example name", "description": "Example description" } }
}

### IAM (authorization/iam): the health check shows that the service runs with the IAM context wired: 204, or a 500 problem document that lists the failing dependencies.
# Every IAM operation requires a bearer token; each one adds its requests to this section.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### Resolve a User service token over REST: 200 with the subject, or resolved = false with the token reason code; 401 without a valid bearer token
# Replace both tokens: the bearer token of the caller (a user token, or a service token that names the IAM caller audience) and the credential to resolve.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/token-resolutions
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "credential": "<token to resolve>"
}

### Resolve a User service token over GraphQL: the same answer as the REST operation; the error code UNAUTHENTICATED without a valid bearer token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($credential: String!) { resolveToken(input: { credential: $credential }) { resolved reason subjectId subjectKind sessionId roles expiresAt } }",
  "variables": { "credential": "<token to resolve>" }
}

### Create a role over REST: 201 with Location, ETag, the id and version 1; 409 for a duplicate name; 422 for an invalid name or a reused Idempotency-Key; 401 without a valid bearer token
# A repeated Idempotency-Key with the same body within 24 hours returns the original result and creates nothing again.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/roles
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Idempotency-Key: create-billing-administrator
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Billing administrator",
  "description": "Manages invoices and refunds."
}

### Create a role over GraphQL: the same data as the REST operation; the error codes CONFLICT, VALIDATION_FAILED and UNAUTHENTICATED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation ($input: CreateRoleInput!) { createRole(input: $input) { id name description kind grantCount version createdAt updatedAt } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "name": "Billing administrator", "description": "Manages invoices and refunds.", "idempotencyKey": "create-billing-administrator" } }
}

### Get a role over REST: 200 with its ETag, 404 for an unknown id, 422 for an id that is not a UUID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/roles/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>

### Get a role over GraphQL: null for an unknown id
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($id: ID!) { role(id: $id) { id name description kind grantCount version createdAt updatedAt } }",
  "variables": { "id": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe" }
}

### Update a role over REST: 200 with the new ETag; 428 without If-Match; 412 for a stale If-Match; 403 for a system role; 404 for an unknown id; 409 for a duplicate name; 422 for invalid fields
# The If-Match header carries the ETag of the version read. A null description removes it and an absent member keeps it.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/roles/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
If-Match: "1"
Idempotency-Key: rename-billing-administrator
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Accounting administrator",
  "description": null
}

### Update a role over GraphQL: the same data as the REST operation; the error codes PRECONDITION_REQUIRED, PRECONDITION_FAILED, FORBIDDEN, NOT_FOUND, CONFLICT and VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation ($input: UpdateRoleInput!) { updateRole(input: $input) { id name description kind grantCount version createdAt updatedAt } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "id": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe", "expectedVersion": 1, "name": "Accounting administrator" } }
}

### List roles over REST: a page of 1 to 100 roles with the nextCursor of the next page, filtered by namePrefix (without regard to case) and kind (system or custom)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/roles?limit=30&namePrefix=bill&kind=custom
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>

### List roles over GraphQL: the same page; pass the nextCursor as after for the next page
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($first: Int, $after: String, $filter: RoleFilter) { roles(first: $first, after: $after, filter: $filter) { items { id name kind grantCount version createdAt updatedAt } nextCursor } }",
  "variables": { "first": 30, "filter": { "namePrefix": "bill", "kind": "custom" } }
}

### Load a GraphQL specification over REST: a draft version with its hash, coordinate count and the diff against the active versions (201); the same SDL again returns that version (200). The service iam is reserved (403); a body is limited to 6 MiB (413)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql-specs
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "service": "billing",
  "sdl": "type Query {\n  invoices: [Invoice!]!\n}\n\ntype Mutation {\n  pay(id: ID!): Invoice! @iamSensitive\n}\n\ntype Invoice {\n  id: ID!\n}\n"
}

### Load a GraphQL specification over GraphQL: the same data as the REST operation; the error codes FORBIDDEN and VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation ($input: LoadGraphqlSpecInput!) { loadGraphqlSpec(input: $input) { id service contentHash status uploadedBy createdAt coordinateCount diff { added removed removedGrants { coordinate roles } wildcardGains { role pattern coordinates } flagDowngrades { coordinate before { sensitive auditAlways } after { sensitive auditAlways } } } } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "service": "billing", "sdl": "type Query { invoices: [String!]! }" } }
}

### Assign a role over REST: 201 with Location, ETag and Iam-Policy-Version; 409 for a duplicate assignment; 422 for an invalid value, an unknown role (roleId) or a past expiry (expiresAt)
# The subject is a user (a UUID) or a service (a service name such as billing-worker); the scope is global or a project (with projectId). A role that grants a wildcard or an iam: key also records iam.privileged_role.assigned.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/user-roles
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Idempotency-Key: assign-billing-administrator
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": { "kind": "user", "id": "0190f2a8-7b3c-7d4e-8f10-1234567890ab" },
  "roleId": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe",
  "scope": { "kind": "project", "projectId": "0190f2a8-7b3c-7d4e-8f10-1234567890cd" },
  "expiresAt": "2099-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}

### Assign a role over GraphQL: the same data as the REST operation; the error codes CONFLICT and VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation ($input: AssignUserRoleInput!) { assignUserRole(input: $input) { id subject { kind id } roleId roleName scope { kind projectId } expiresAt version createdAt updatedAt } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "subject": { "kind": "service", "id": "billing-worker" }, "roleId": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe", "scope": { "kind": "global" } } }
}

### Read an assignment over REST: 200 with the ETag and the role name; 404 for an unknown or revoked assignment
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user-roles/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facff
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>

### Read an assignment over GraphQL: null for an unknown or revoked assignment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($id: ID!) { userRole(id: $id) { id subject { kind id } roleId roleName scope { kind projectId } expiresAt version createdAt updatedAt } }",
  "variables": { "id": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facff" }
}

### List assignments over REST: a page of 1 to 100 assignments with the nextCursor of the next page, filtered by subjectKind, subjectId, roleId, projectId and includeExpired
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user-roles?limit=30&subjectKind=service&includeExpired=false
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>

### List assignments over GraphQL: the same page; pass the nextCursor as after for the next page
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($first: Int, $after: String, $filter: UserRoleFilter) { userRoles(first: $first, after: $after, filter: $filter) { items { id subject { kind id } roleId roleName scope { kind projectId } expiresAt version createdAt updatedAt } nextCursor } }",
  "variables": { "first": 30, "filter": { "subjectKind": "service", "includeExpired": false } }
}
